<div class="system-frame">
    <div class="corner-tag top-left">SYS.LOC // 0x77B</div>
    <div class="corner-tag bottom-right">v2.12_RECURSION</div>

    <header class="schema-header">
        <div class="sys-status">
            <span>Circuit: Non-Linear Temporal Synthesis</span>
            <span>Status: [UNLOCKED]</span>
        </div>
        <div class="title-group">
            <h1>recursive sonic engine</h1>
            <span class="scientific-subtitle">Aion vs Chronos // Eternal Return</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-container">
        
        <div class="theory-block">
            <p><strong>[ABSTRACT]</strong> This module charts the engineering of a digital audio looper treated not as a passive capturing device, but as an intensive desiring-machine. By capturing live instrumentation within memory-mapped circular structures, the engine violently breaks linear history (Chronos), routing audio flows into a flat, interconnected plane of pure multiplicity and repetition (Aion).</p>
            
            <div class="highlight-box">
                // CRITICAL MATRIX: The loop is never the return of the same. Every digital cycle registers an active affirmation of difference—an accumulation of speed, layers, and intensive sound states that escape teleological capture.
            </div>

            <p style="margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--accent-orange);">[Anatomy of the Feed-Forward Machine]</p>
            
            <p><strong>1. The Circuit (Circular Buffer):</strong> At the micro-layer, time is bound into a fixed sample ring. The current position index crawls across a predetermined duration of memory, wrapping immediately back to zero the moment it encounters the limit. It is a mathematical manifestation of the Eternal Return—forcing the past to coexist directly with the present in a constant state of intensive layering.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. The Rupture (Hotkey Time-Anomalies):</strong> Rather than allowing the audio pointer to drift progressively forward, a customized hotkey architecture enables instantaneous, sample-accurate re-indexing. Tapping a node shatters chronological alignment, forcefully jumping the read head across different spatial fields of the recorded phrase to create a shattered, non-linear rhythmic distribution.</p>
            
            <p><strong>3. The Interception (Decoupled Frequency Mapping):</strong> To ensure the audio output remains continuous, a secondary processing thread extracts raw frames from the buffer without locking the real-time stream. These extracted frames are passed to a background analytical algorithm that decodes changing musical patterns and calculates root harmonic variations on the fly.</p>
        </div>

